      "title": "Computing a Probability at a Point"
    },
    "markdown": "Given $X∼\\text{Po}(5),$ compute $P(X=3),$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
    "mathAcademyId": "q-130050",
    "preview": true,
    "requiresCalculator": null,
    "solution": "If $X∼\\text{Po}(\\lambda ),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Po}(5),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{5}^{x}{e}^{-5}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{3}{e}^{-5}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.1404.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "status": "incorrect",
